Assessment
Endocrinology chart review - A1c result. 75-year-old man (DOB 1948-09-21, MRN SYN-1972686), T2DM since 2009, HTN, lives alone, still drives. A1c trajectory: 10.4% (2023-11-15) -> 7.6% (2024-02-20) -> 6.2% (2024-05-29). Regimen: insulin glargine started 10 u qHS 2023-11-20 with self-titration (+2 u q3d to FBG 100-130); patient self-titrated to 30 u qHS. Also metformin 1000 mg BID, sitagliptin 100 mg daily; HCTZ 25 mg daily. Diabetes RN phone call 2024-05-30: frequent lows; severe nocturnal hypoglycemia 2024-05-26 03:10 (BG 48, sweating/confused, required neighbor assistance); 14-day meter FBG 58-84 mg/dL with 5 readings <70. Weight down 4 kg since January, no missed meals, no alcohol. Cr 1.0, eGFR 76, Hgb 14.2 (A1c reliable).
Assessment: A1c 6.2% represents over-treatment with basal insulin in an older adult with recurrent and severe (level 3) nocturnal hypoglycemia. Risk factors: age 75, lives alone, drives, insulin therapy, weight loss/improved diet reducing insulin requirement, prior unsupervised self-titration. Individualized A1c target <7.5% (avoid hypoglycemia; fasting goal ~100-150 mg/dL). Metformin and sitagliptin carry minimal hypoglycemia risk and are continued;
